{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Are brought down. You recline.</b> It is possible that it is a past-tense verb, like אשר ילד לו (Genesis 35:26), and it is possible that it is future in place of past, in masculine form, like ולקח מהם קללה (Jeremiah 29:22), and this is an elegant usage; likewise in the language of Kedar, and so ומכסך, and it is a verb:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:44.101057943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}